A||||6||qwikgta||FREE......Rear Strut....How To Do It Yourself||||10||
Z||000000||qwikgta||07-15-2001||11:04 PM||||I know that some folks on this forum sell parts that do the same thing and I do not want to step on their toes.   <BR>  With that said, I was looking to put a rear strut on my coupe.  See I put a spoiler on the back and then my trunk would not stay up.  Now, I looked into buying a rear strut kit but I figured that this was too easy to not do it myself.  So I took some measurements and went to the local J-yard.  After removing many struts I finally found one.  So here it is.  <BR>  To put a strut on the back of your trunk you will need a 84 Buick Regal front hood strut.  I got mine FREE from the yard becasue the guy said that there is no money in a used strut.  You can get them new for about $16.00.  <BR>  After you get it remove the front most hood bolt (to you as you look at the open trunk) on the driver side, and place the skinny end on the bolt.  I used a 40mm bolt here (replaced the stock 30mm bolt) and some washers on the inside.  Then place the other end on the small bracket that is located on the driver side strut well.  It is below the strut bolt area by about 4-5 inchs.  You may have Cruise Control parts on or near this bracket.  I have no cruise control so this bracket was not being used.  Anyway you need to slightly bend the bracket so it will allow you to put the strut end on it and still have some range of motion. <BR>  That is it, I did it for free and it took me 5 minutes to put it on.  It holds the trunk at any hight and has no clearance probs with the engine cover.  <P>  I will be in Williamsburg, VA in Aug if you want to see it on the car, I don't have my Digicam to take any photos.  If I do get a chance to get some pics I will post them.  <P>  Again, I thought I would post this info to you because I believe that is the spirit of this forum, help out others.  Sorry if this takes money out of some pockets.<P>Rob<P>------------------<BR>qwikgta@yahoo.com<BR>88 T-Top coupe, 65K, Header no Cat, 16" GTZ rims, short shifter, swaybar, open element air cleaner, hood vents.<BR>http://www.homestead.com/robsfieroproject   <BR>http://www.vafieros.com<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigpic2.jpg"> ||||reg||10
Z||000001||Steve Normington||07-15-2001||11:07 PM||||Is the car that you did this to, the one in your signature? Spoilers/luggage racks can make a difference on how much force you need. How fast does the lid go up when you pop it?||||reg||1
