Z||000003||BV MotorSports||07-16-2001||10:33 PM||||Very good info. Yesterday I went to close my trunk and heard a loud "pop", opened it up and found the decklid rod on the pass side snapped. Since GM used a stupid tamper resistant star bolt holding it on I had to use a pair of vise grips to get what was left of the arm and bracket off. Now my trunk lid is WAY too heavy to lift! To think its going to stay up with just 1 good rod will have me either going to the hospital when the trunk lid comes down and knocks me out cold (has almost happened b4!) or rubbing a big knot on my head.<BR>I'd like to see what you did and how much extra force is added.<P>Steven<P>------------------<BR>87 Fiero GT 14.9/ 89mph<BR>94 Formula WS6 w/ NOS 12.4 /118mph<BR>87 Conquest TSi <BR>87 Conquest TSi 406 SBC V8!<BR>85.5 Starion ESi||||reg||11
