Z||000005||qwikgta||07-19-2001||07:01 AM||||Sorry, I have been offline for a few days.  The strut holds the trunk lid very tight at any angle i put the lid in.  Also, when it is up the wind cannot blow it down.  It is working great, again, I used a "used" strut and it is working perfect, if you get a new one it may hold better.  I still have all the original parts on the car for the lid, this just helps it.  I will be in Williamsburg for the "big show" if anyone wants to see it first hand.  <P>PS- Yes, it is on my 88 coupe in my sig.<P>Rob <P>------------------<BR>qwikgta@yahoo.com<BR>88 T-Top coupe, 65K, Header no Cat, 16" GTZ rims, short shifter, swaybar, open element air cleaner, hood vents.<BR>http://www.homestead.com/robsfieroproject   <BR>http://www.vafieros.com<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigpic2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||grinthock||07-19-2001||07:05 AM||||If you want EASY get rodney's strut, it's WAY better quality then those PepBoyz struts, he told me he uses Industrial Grade struts, and his kit installins in 2 minutes....  I took my old torsion bars out, kind a pain the screw was a pain to get out, I couldn't turn it, Oh well, just drilled it out and it came right off||||reg||10
